171 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (This project aims to develop an Automated Training Framework to compare different learning-rate schedules and hyperparameter configurations for deep neural networks. The framework will be implemented using Python and PyTorch on Google Colab, with GPU acceleration. The CIFAR-10 dataset will be used to train a Convolutional Neural Network \(CNN\) for image classification. Different learning-rate schedules, including Constant, Warmup, Cosine Annealing and One-Cycle, will be tested along with hyperparameters such as learning rate, batch size, epochs and optimizers. The performance of different configurations will be evaluated using accuracy, loss and training time. Matplotlib and TensorBoard will be used to visualize and monitor the experimental results. The main objective is to identify the most effective training configuration and make deep learning experimentation more automated and efficient.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
