177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (Deep learning models require suitable training configurations to achieve better performance and accuracy. The learning rate, optimizer, batch size and other hyperparameters significantly influence the training process. Selecting the right combination of these settings often requires multiple experiments. This project develops an Automated Training Framework using Python, PyTorch and Google Colab to simplify this process. A Convolutional Neural Network \(CNN\) is trained using the CIFAR-10 dataset with different learning-rate schedules and hyperparameter configurations. The framework automatically conducts experiments, evaluates model performance and compares results using accuracy, loss and training time. It also generates graphs and reports to identify the most effective training configuration.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
